579
00:32:29,770 --> 00:32:32,390
Hm? Hm? Hm? Hm? Hm? Hm?

580
00:32:32,390 --> 00:32:34,090
This one doesn't go dark?

581
00:32:34,090 --> 00:32:36,430
Wow, the lights are so clean

582
00:32:36,430 --> 00:32:37,150
S-so clean

583
00:32:37,150 --> 00:32:39,350
Hm? Hm? Hm?

584
00:32:39,350 --> 00:32:41,630
Oh, it's just the lights getting old

585
00:32:41,630 --> 00:32:42,510
Okay, okay, okay

586
00:32:42,510 --> 00:32:44,210
Alright, alright

587
00:32:44,210 --> 00:32:46,350
It was just the "lights getting old" type

588
00:32:46,350 --> 00:32:48,010
Oh thank goodness

589
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:51,270
It was so clean

590
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:52,470
Moving on

591
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:54,190
Phew

592
00:32:54,190 --> 00:33:00,830
The tiles are so cute

593
00:33:00,830 --> 00:33:07,560
The tiles are cute

594
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:12,540
To think I'd be praising your tiles

595
00:33:12,540 --> 00:33:13,020
Hahaha

596
00:33:13,020 --> 00:33:15,740
Hahaha

597
00:33:15,740 --> 00:33:26,030
Let me push through here and take a look first

598
00:33:26,030 --> 00:33:30,810
I wonder if the anomalies narrow down

599
00:33:30,810 --> 00:33:34,270
Do I need to clear it first?

600
00:33:34,270 --> 00:33:42,410
Right, if I don't reset, maybe new ones will show up too

601
00:33:42,410 --> 00:33:47,270
Not sure, but it's fun so let's reset

602
00:33:47,270 --> 00:33:49,270
Reset

603
00:33:49,270 --> 00:33:55,820
Oh really? If I go this far...

604
00:33:55,820 --> 00:33:57,700
Huh?

605
00:33:57,700 --> 00:34:05,790
Oh, it doesn't count unless I turn back. Right.

606
00:34:05,790 --> 00:34:11,080
I'm starting to get confused

607
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:20,480
Oh, that's right. The current one is weird so I can just turn back

608
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:23,440
This is correct. Correct.

609
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:26,600
But when it turns out to be wrong, that's the worst

610
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:34,290
It's so frustrating, like what was the anomaly? This is right, right? This is right, right?

611
00:34:34,290 --> 00:34:39,480
Okay, going in

612
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:44,230
Yes, correct. Alright.

613
00:34:44,230 --> 00:34:50,990
So I'm going back in from 0. Was the no-smoking poster here before?

614
00:34:50,990 --> 00:35:06,680
Oh, what's this?

615
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:12,380
Is it just going in reverse?

616
00:35:12,380 --> 00:35:16,140
It's reversed — wait, is the path just flipped?

617
00:35:16,140 --> 00:35:22,770
Huh? This? Hm?

618
00:35:22,770 --> 00:35:27,360
It was just reversed

619
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:30,230
That surprised me

620
00:35:30,230 --> 00:35:41,270
I thought I'd be lost forever from that one

621
00:35:41,270 --> 00:35:48,350
Only two lights went out. Maybe more go out as you walk further?

622
00:35:48,570 --> 00:35:58,310
Can I get one more?

623
00:35:58,310 --> 00:36:09,500
Okay, stopping

624
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:13,360
Getting scared. I'm stopping.

625
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:19,440
Turned back

626
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:24,740
Turning them all off is scary

627
00:36:24,740 --> 00:36:31,100
I don't want to turn them all off, that'd be terrifying

628
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:36,220
Moving on! Today I want to see all the anomalies

629
00:36:36,220 --> 00:36:49,360
So I'll keep an eye out for new anomalies too

630
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:57,050
Normal old man

631
00:36:57,050 --> 00:37:00,770
But wait, what if there are like 100 anomalies or something?

632
00:37:00,770 --> 00:37:08,140
Ooh! What's this about the tactile paving blocks?

633
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:12,740
It's so smooth! Wait — is that a face? Like...

634
00:37:12,740 --> 00:37:19,210
Someone got their face pressed into the tactile paving blocks while they were being installed

635
00:37:19,210 --> 00:37:23,990
Maybe that's it? Like while the cement on the tactile blocks was still wet

636
00:37:23,990 --> 00:37:28,290
With a face going "nngh, nngh, nngh"

637
00:37:28,290 --> 00:37:34,150
Someone got pressed into it. So many times too

638
00:37:34,150 --> 00:37:38,570
That's the anomaly. It goes up to here. From here someone's face is pressed in

639
00:37:38,570 --> 00:37:43,290
It doesn't really look like a face when you look closely. Amazing

640
00:37:43,290 --> 00:37:46,180
It's like going "uuuugh"

641
00:37:46,180 --> 00:37:52,470
Alright, I'm heading back.

642
00:37:52,470 --> 00:37:57,250
Okay, how many left?

643
00:37:57,250 --> 00:38:02,090
17 more — we've cut it down quite a bit!

644
00:38:02,090 --> 00:38:05,980
Here we go.

645
00:38:05,980 --> 00:38:08,640
Okay!

646
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:28,250
Oh, sorry, never mind — I thought something seemed off.

647
00:38:28,250 --> 00:38:34,960
Nope, it's normal.

648
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:45,170
Anomalies I remember... what else was there?

649
00:38:45,170 --> 00:38:51,540
Like the uncle smiling...

650
00:38:51,540 --> 00:38:56,020
I don't know, I feel like there was another Shining-type one.

651
00:38:56,020 --> 00:39:00,230
Let's go! Here we go!

652
00:39:01,290 --> 00:39:03,350
That's not a drain.

653
00:39:03,350 --> 00:39:05,580
Two vents.

654
00:39:05,580 --> 00:39:06,930
Three.

655
00:39:06,930 --> 00:39:08,270
Tiles.

656
00:39:08,270 --> 00:39:11,300
Doorknob.

657
00:39:11,300 --> 00:39:13,080
The guy looks normal.

658
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:16,120
What's wrong with the guy smiling?

659
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:16,880
Do you remember this one?

660
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:18,180
Do you remember this part changing?

661
00:39:18,180 --> 00:39:20,240
I feel like the lights were weird too.

662
00:39:20,240 --> 00:39:22,560
Nope.

663
00:39:22,560 --> 00:39:28,830
Nothing, right?

664
00:39:28,830 --> 00:39:30,790
Like the doorknob disappearing...

665
00:39:30,790 --> 00:39:34,270
Shall we go?

666
00:39:34,270 --> 00:39:37,260
Yep.

667
00:39:37,260 --> 00:39:40,280
Give me an anomaly, come on!

668
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:43,770
In search of anomalies...

669
00:39:43,770 --> 00:39:44,570
Alright then.

670
00:39:44,570 --> 00:39:46,350
Off we go!

671
00:39:46,350 --> 00:39:52,480
Feet — check.

672
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:53,920
No smoking sign — check.

673
00:39:53,920 --> 00:39:57,380
Poster — check.

674
00:39:57,380 --> 00:40:02,000
Oh, it's open!

675
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Aaaaaaah!

676
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:10,790
Did you see that?

677
00:40:10,790 --> 00:40:26,970
Nothing in particular.

678
00:40:26,970 --> 00:40:29,670
Nothing at all.

679
00:40:29,670 --> 00:40:33,670
Wasn't it supposed to do something when you look at it?

680
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:43,420
If it doesn't do anything, I'll forget about it — that's scary.

681
00:40:43,420 --> 00:40:49,020
Okay, let's go!

682
00:40:51,220 --> 00:40:55,140
Six posters.

683
00:40:55,140 --> 00:40:55,940
Nearby...

684
00:40:55,940 --> 00:40:57,840
Two.

685
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:59,660
Nothing at a glance.

686
00:40:59,660 --> 00:41:02,040
At a glance, yeah.

687
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:04,200
It's just a quick look, after all.

688
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:05,560
Oh, he's smiling!

689
00:41:05,560 --> 00:41:08,040
There he is — the smiling uncle!

690
00:41:08,040 --> 00:41:10,850
Something good must've happened.

691
00:41:10,850 --> 00:41:15,180
There it is!

692
00:41:15,180 --> 00:41:16,400
Smiling uncle!

693
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:18,120
Something good must've happened.

694
00:41:18,120 --> 00:41:19,500
Hey~

695
00:41:19,500 --> 00:41:20,840
Alright Polka, let's head back.

696
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:22,900
You're an anomaly, you know.

697
00:41:22,900 --> 00:41:24,340
Yeah, you're an anomaly.

698
00:41:24,340 --> 00:41:27,360
I wonder when you'll stop smiling.

699
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:30,160
Mister, mister~

700
00:41:30,160 --> 00:41:33,120
When are you gonna stop smiling?

701
00:41:33,120 --> 00:41:37,310
I'm curious.

702
00:41:37,310 --> 00:41:45,500
I really want to see the moment this guy stops smiling.

703
00:41:45,500 --> 00:41:47,210
Ah, still smiling.

704
00:41:47,210 --> 00:41:51,640
That startled me.

705
00:41:51,640 --> 00:41:53,280
I thought the smile was gone for a second.

706
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:57,450
Phew, good.

707
00:41:57,450 --> 00:42:00,150
Oh, oh, oh!

708
00:42:00,150 --> 00:42:01,610
He says he ate sushi!

709
00:42:01,610 --> 00:42:08,000
Alright!

710
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:09,740
On to the next one.

711
00:42:09,740 --> 00:42:15,660
Clearing, clearing.

712
00:42:15,660 --> 00:42:16,650
Here we go, yes.

713
00:42:16,650 --> 00:42:21,570
Oh my~

714
00:42:21,570 --> 00:42:22,490
Something...

715
00:42:22,490 --> 00:42:23,670
Over there.

716
00:42:23,670 --> 00:42:24,750
It's open.

717
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:26,350
Is this the right answer?

718
00:42:26,350 --> 00:42:32,460
No way!

719
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:36,750
Polka, this one...

720
00:42:36,750 --> 00:42:37,690
I'm pretty sure at first...

721
00:42:37,690 --> 00:42:40,030
On the 8th loop,

722
00:42:40,030 --> 00:42:42,670
right when I thought it was almost over,

723
00:42:42,670 --> 00:42:44,170
I think I drew the fake exit.

724
00:42:44,170 --> 00:42:45,970
The fake exit.

725
00:42:45,970 --> 00:42:50,050
But it was Exit 0, right?

726
00:42:50,050 --> 00:42:52,070
I'm not going in there.

727
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:54,330
That's an anomaly.

728
00:42:54,330 --> 00:42:57,270
So Polka just casually

729
00:42:57,270 --> 00:42:59,730
thought it was the end, looked left, and it said Exit 0 —

730
00:42:59,730 --> 00:43:00,450
I was genuinely freaked out.

731
00:43:00,450 --> 00:43:06,180
14 more to go.

732
00:43:06,180 --> 00:43:06,760
Alright!

733
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:08,720
Let's go!

734
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:11,820
And Polka starts walking!

735
00:43:11,820 --> 00:43:13,980
No anomalies so far.

736
00:43:13,980 --> 00:43:17,080
The fest has

737
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:19,120
started up too.

738
00:43:19,120 --> 00:43:21,340
It's the underground plaza.

739
00:43:21,340 --> 00:43:25,020
This guy is really

740
00:43:25,020 --> 00:43:25,720
looking all over the place.

741
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:26,960
He's looking at me!

742
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:28,900
Homing missile old man!

743
00:43:28,900 --> 00:43:37,660
Don't fire the homing, don't fire the homing, don't fire it — wait wait wait — homing, homing, homing, homing, homing, homing, homing!

744
00:43:37,660 --> 00:43:41,500
He's watching me, watching me, watching me — I give up here.

745
00:43:41,500 --> 00:43:43,300
His neck can't actually twist that far.

746
00:43:43,300 --> 00:43:46,050
But he keeps looking at me?

747
00:43:46,050 --> 00:43:47,900
How long are you gonna keep staring at me?

748
00:43:47,900 --> 00:43:50,500
How long?!

749
00:44:00,740 --> 00:44:03,300
Fine, go ahead and look at your phone.

750
00:44:03,300 --> 00:44:05,960
My back is totally exposed now.

751
00:44:05,960 --> 00:44:08,560
What are you even tapping on that thing?

752
00:44:08,560 --> 00:44:12,280
Well, you'd stare — Polka is cute after all, can't blame you.

753
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:15,660
Why hello there~

754
00:44:15,660 --> 00:44:18,520
His neck is gonna snap.

755
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:21,340
Aww, he's hanging his head.

756
00:44:21,340 --> 00:44:25,840
Hey hey, it's Exit 8!

757
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:27,360
Let's go home.

758
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:31,020
Here we go.

759
00:44:31,020 --> 00:44:31,520
Okay.

760
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:41,180
Once this is done, won't it be over?

761
00:44:41,180 --> 00:44:44,760
Is it ending?

762
00:44:44,760 --> 00:44:48,020
Hello? Excuse me, sir, is it ending?

763
00:44:48,020 --> 00:44:51,240
So,

764
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:54,840
Polka is judging this as no anomaly and

765
00:44:54,840 --> 00:44:59,480
is going to turn back and reset one more time.

766
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:00,900
Seriously though,

767
00:45:00,900 --> 00:45:03,020
if there WAS an anomaly here,

768
00:45:03,020 --> 00:45:06,080
that'd be pretty funny.

769
00:45:06,080 --> 00:45:09,180
Polka not noticing and there being an anomaly again...

770
00:45:09,180 --> 00:45:12,340
Alright!

771
00:45:12,340 --> 00:45:20,270
Okay, reset done!

772
00:45:20,270 --> 00:45:21,450
13 more to go.

773
00:45:21,450 --> 00:45:23,830
Off I go!

774
00:45:23,830 --> 00:45:26,670
Thank goodness.

775
00:45:26,670 --> 00:45:29,610
Polka has safely cleared all the anomaly checks so far.

776
00:45:29,610 --> 00:45:30,450
Moving on.

777
00:45:30,450 --> 00:45:39,170
The old man...

778
00:45:39,170 --> 00:45:57,170
Wait, could it be an anomaly that the old man is absent because I turned back?

779
00:45:57,170 --> 00:46:02,790
Is this an anomaly?

780
00:46:02,790 --> 00:46:08,230
The old man was on his way back and then suddenly —

781
00:46:08,230 --> 00:46:15,160
Oh wait, did I reset too many times?

782
00:46:15,160 --> 00:46:17,880
Could it be that the "old man missing" anomaly

783
00:46:18,560 --> 00:46:20,960
is one this pro is bad at handling?

784
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:21,540
Maybe?

785
00:46:21,540 --> 00:46:27,720
Up to here...

786
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:29,160
Oh, okay okay okay!

787
00:46:29,160 --> 00:46:30,960
Phew.

788
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:33,820
Okay okay okay!

789
00:46:33,820 --> 00:46:34,700
From here on.

790
00:46:34,700 --> 00:46:37,120
I was feeling lonely that the old man wasn't coming...

791
00:46:37,120 --> 00:46:38,280
Okay.

792
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:40,990
He came!

793
00:46:40,990 --> 00:46:45,830
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6...

794
00:46:45,830 --> 00:46:47,310
Let's keep moving.

795
00:46:47,310 --> 00:46:50,250
Three rooms.

796
00:46:50,250 --> 00:46:54,510
The painting looks creepy.

797
00:46:54,510 --> 00:47:00,660
Polka's not visible in it.

798
00:47:00,660 --> 00:47:03,080
They made it into a creepy painting?

799
00:47:03,080 --> 00:47:04,360
W-who's that?

800
00:47:04,360 --> 00:47:06,440
Oh, it's the lady from the fest!

801
00:47:06,440 --> 00:47:06,860
Let's go back.

802
00:47:06,860 --> 00:47:10,830
The old guy turned into a scary painting.

803
00:47:10,830 --> 00:47:17,270
The festival lady disappeared!

804
00:47:17,270 --> 00:47:21,510
What did she draw?

805
00:47:21,510 --> 00:47:25,310
Moving on!

806
00:47:25,310 --> 00:47:26,890
Okay.

807
00:47:26,890 --> 00:47:30,250
Pretty normal.

808
00:47:30,250 --> 00:47:32,070
Isn't today's old guy bigger than usual?

809
00:47:32,070 --> 00:47:36,330
Is there a spot where he keeps getting bigger?

810
00:47:36,330 --> 00:47:37,050
Was there something like that?

811
00:47:37,050 --> 00:47:38,950
Like, isn't today's old guy huge?

812
00:47:38,950 --> 00:47:43,050
The placard is getting smaller.

813
00:47:43,050 --> 00:47:44,270
Wait, the old guy is huge—

814
00:47:44,270 --> 00:47:44,910
Hold on.

815
00:47:44,910 --> 00:47:46,310
What the—

816
00:47:46,310 --> 00:47:49,110
The old guy keeps getting bigger!

817
00:47:49,110 --> 00:47:52,820
That's scary!

818
00:47:52,820 --> 00:47:54,340
What is this?

819
00:47:54,340 --> 00:47:56,180
Which one is changing?

820
00:47:56,180 --> 00:47:57,900
The old guy is getting massive!

821
00:47:57,900 --> 00:47:59,040
Huh?

822
00:47:59,040 --> 00:48:01,730
This is so unsettling.

823
00:48:01,730 --> 00:48:03,980
I've been seeing him this whole time, and now—

824
00:48:03,980 --> 00:48:07,270
—he suddenly gets huge, it's terrifying!

825
00:48:07,270 --> 00:48:10,100
He's so big now!

826
00:48:10,100 --> 00:48:17,130
I've never seen him from this angle before.

827
00:48:17,130 --> 00:48:21,310
Good work!

828
00:48:21,310 --> 00:48:26,720
Polka's scale stays the same, right?

829
00:48:26,720 --> 00:48:28,780
Oh, right!

830
00:48:28,780 --> 00:48:30,880
Only the old guy changed!

831
00:48:30,880 --> 00:48:33,140
Alright!

832
00:48:33,140 --> 00:48:37,580
They say boys grow up fast if you don't see them for two days.

833
00:48:37,580 --> 00:48:39,080
It hasn't even been two days though!

834
00:48:39,080 --> 00:48:40,260
Or has it?

835
00:48:40,260 --> 00:48:43,820
There was something like that in Jujutsu Kaisen too.

836
00:48:43,820 --> 00:48:44,740
Let's go!

837
00:48:44,740 --> 00:48:54,950
And then Polka gets hit by a laser—

838
00:48:54,950 --> 00:48:55,870
—and dies!

839
00:48:55,870 --> 00:49:06,150
Bye bye!

840
00:49:06,150 --> 00:49:07,630
See ya!

841
00:49:07,630 --> 00:49:09,790
But for the fire hydrant—

842
00:49:09,790 --> 00:49:12,070
If the light was off, you wouldn't be able to tell, right?

843
00:49:12,070 --> 00:49:21,490
Here we go, here we go.

844
00:49:21,490 --> 00:49:29,940
10 more.

845
00:49:29,940 --> 00:49:31,700
10 more.

846
00:49:31,700 --> 00:49:33,400
10 more.

847
00:49:33,400 --> 00:49:35,420
10 more.

848
00:49:35,420 --> 00:49:44,670
Lights, normal.

849
00:49:44,670 --> 00:49:46,670
Floor, normal. No smoking sign.

850
00:49:46,670 --> 00:49:49,430
Poster.

851
00:49:49,430 --> 00:49:50,270
Poster.

852
00:49:50,270 --> 00:49:53,090
Old guy.

853
00:49:53,090 --> 00:49:55,150
Old guy? Old guy? Old guy?

854
00:49:55,150 --> 00:49:58,830
Underground plaza? Underground plaza? Underground plaza?

855
00:49:58,830 --> 00:49:59,570
Nothing wrong, right?

856
00:49:59,570 --> 00:50:05,370
Oh yeah!

857
00:50:05,370 --> 00:50:06,930
Really? What do you all think?

