01:04:27,290 --> 01:04:30,090
Hey, aren't there more posters than before?

1137
01:04:30,090 --> 01:04:32,090
Are you okay?

1138
01:04:32,090 --> 01:04:43,200
Can't read it, can't read it.

1139
01:04:43,200 --> 01:04:44,710
Exit 8...

1140
01:04:44,710 --> 01:04:46,070
Exit 8...

1141
01:04:46,070 --> 01:04:47,770
It's the Exit 8 sign!

1142
01:04:47,770 --> 01:04:49,030
Don't run.

1143
01:04:49,030 --> 01:04:50,290
Wait a moment.

1144
01:04:50,290 --> 01:04:52,270
Back to the knee— wait, back up.

1145
01:04:52,270 --> 01:04:54,550
Are you okay?

1146
01:04:54,550 --> 01:04:56,650
Exit 8...

1147
01:04:56,650 --> 01:04:59,270
Go back, go back, go back!

1148
01:04:59,270 --> 01:05:00,870
Isn't this new?

1149
01:05:00,870 --> 01:05:02,450
Was that there before?

1150
01:05:02,450 --> 01:05:04,210
Was there ever a poster like that?

1151
01:05:06,010 --> 01:05:14,740
First time seeing it — so there's one more left.

1152
01:05:14,740 --> 01:05:23,780
Alright everyone, let's go! So that means... Polka might know what the last anomaly is!

1153
01:05:23,780 --> 01:05:31,910
I might've figured it out!

1154
01:05:31,910 --> 01:05:45,610
Maybe the world is flipped!

1155
01:05:46,130 --> 01:05:50,150
Like, this one...

1156
01:05:50,150 --> 01:05:56,810
I love this kind of thing — a curveball, something weird, a sense of wrongness.

1157
01:05:56,810 --> 01:06:01,990
The rocks, the clanging...

1158
01:06:01,990 --> 01:06:04,550
And so—

1159
01:06:04,550 --> 01:06:10,510
Yes! All anomalies have been found. "Thank you very much for using this passage—"

1160
01:06:10,510 --> 01:06:15,210
"Thank you very much." Well, it's not exactly a clear, but sort of!

1161
01:06:15,210 --> 01:06:21,930
Now, everyone's favorite anomalies will appear in random order!

1162
01:06:21,930 --> 01:06:26,150
So exciting! I wonder what's coming!

1163
01:06:26,150 --> 01:06:28,830
What's gonna show up?

1164
01:06:28,830 --> 01:06:35,130
Okay, these are anomalies we've already seen, so Polka should be fine — you'll spot them right away, right?

1165
01:06:35,130 --> 01:06:39,050
Is the guy small? No, that doesn't seem right.

1166
01:06:39,050 --> 01:06:43,120
Two passages.

1167
01:06:43,120 --> 01:06:46,000
The guy looks tough.

1168
01:06:46,080 --> 01:06:50,060
But the plaza — the mental image isn't moving.

1169
01:06:50,060 --> 01:07:08,520
There's a door. Moving on!

1170
01:07:08,520 --> 01:07:12,140
Maybe I can't get out.

1171
01:07:12,140 --> 01:07:15,730
Poster?

1172
01:07:15,730 --> 01:07:19,630
I got too cocky.

1173
01:07:19,630 --> 01:07:22,840
That's what I get for getting cocky.

1174
01:07:22,840 --> 01:07:24,810
That's what I get for getting cocky.

1175
01:07:24,810 --> 01:07:29,370
Can I make it?

1176
01:07:29,370 --> 01:07:33,910
I can go!

1177
01:07:33,910 --> 01:07:39,250
Poster...

1178
01:07:39,250 --> 01:07:40,390
Poster...

1179
01:07:40,390 --> 01:07:43,010
It's not bigger.

1180
01:07:43,010 --> 01:07:47,230
Nothing on top.

1181
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:48,430
No stain.

1182
01:07:48,430 --> 01:07:49,310
The guy...

1183
01:07:49,310 --> 01:07:50,070
The guy...

1184
01:07:50,070 --> 01:07:51,330
Normal-looking guy.

1185
01:07:51,330 --> 01:07:52,610
Door...

1186
01:07:52,610 --> 01:07:53,410
Door...

1187
01:07:53,410 --> 01:07:55,110
The door area looks fine.

1188
01:07:55,110 --> 01:07:57,410
Mental Man...

1189
01:07:57,410 --> 01:07:57,950
Mental Man...

1190
01:07:57,950 --> 01:07:58,630
Mental Man...

1191
01:07:58,630 --> 01:07:58,870
Not there.

1192
01:07:58,870 --> 01:08:08,460
Okay!

1193
01:08:08,460 --> 01:08:11,280
Moving on!

1194
01:08:11,280 --> 01:08:13,880
Alright.

1195
01:08:13,880 --> 01:08:16,440
Umm...

1196
01:08:16,440 --> 01:08:17,060
No smoking sign...

1197
01:08:17,060 --> 01:08:19,360
Poster...

1198
01:08:19,360 --> 01:08:20,940
Normal.

1199
01:08:20,940 --> 01:08:22,780
Yep, normal.

1200
01:08:22,780 --> 01:08:24,040
Normal.

1201
01:08:24,040 --> 01:08:24,920
Normal...

1202
01:08:24,920 --> 01:08:25,960
Looks normal...

1203
01:08:25,960 --> 01:08:26,920
Normal guy...

1204
01:08:26,920 --> 01:08:28,900
Normal guy...

1205
01:08:28,900 --> 01:08:30,460
Normal...

1206
01:08:30,460 --> 01:08:32,280
Normal...

1207
01:08:32,280 --> 01:08:33,920
Normal floor...

1208
01:08:33,920 --> 01:08:35,200
Normal head...

1209
01:08:35,200 --> 01:08:37,560
Normal sign...

1210
01:08:37,560 --> 01:08:38,240
Okay!

1211
01:08:38,240 --> 01:08:43,310
Okay, let's go!

1212
01:08:43,310 --> 01:08:46,150
I'm getting nervous...

1213
01:08:46,150 --> 01:08:49,990
Once you mess up, it gets scary.

1214
01:08:49,990 --> 01:08:50,410
Alright.

1215
01:08:50,410 --> 01:08:59,660
1, 2, 3...

1216
01:08:59,660 --> 01:09:03,460
Normal...

1217
01:09:03,460 --> 01:09:04,300
Poster...

1218
01:09:04,300 --> 01:09:06,600
Normal guy...

1219
01:09:06,600 --> 01:09:08,700
Normal door...

1220
01:09:08,700 --> 01:09:11,040
Normal eyeball...

1221
01:09:11,040 --> 01:09:30,800
Polka might be bad at this.

1222
01:09:30,800 --> 01:09:32,920
I can't tell...

1223
01:09:32,920 --> 01:09:39,720
I wish they made it a bit more obvious.

1224
01:09:47,600 --> 01:09:50,460
The simulacra effect — today's...

1225
01:09:50,460 --> 01:09:55,630
I'm going back.

1226
01:09:55,630 --> 01:09:57,630
That one's hard.

1227
01:09:57,630 --> 01:10:02,370
Which one did everyone find the hardest?

1228
01:10:02,370 --> 01:10:06,370
Watching it in a stream versus actually playing it yourself might feel a bit different too.

1229
01:10:06,370 --> 01:10:08,370
Also, on Switch—

1230
01:10:08,370 --> 01:10:11,370
The Switch version of Exit 8 got more content added, right?

1231
01:10:11,370 --> 01:10:14,370
Apparently there's some kind of Switch-exclusive chapter or something.

1232
01:10:14,370 --> 01:10:18,370
What?! Why are they adding Switch exclusives?!

1233
01:10:18,370 --> 01:10:27,790
I mean, if we're talking hard to notice — the floor tile one was really hard. The one that looks like a face, right?

1234
01:10:27,790 --> 01:10:34,470
Okay. I heard there were Switch-exclusive anomalies, but maybe that was wrong?

1235
01:10:34,470 --> 01:10:39,490
Maybe I'm thinking of something else.

1236
01:10:39,490 --> 01:10:43,400
The eyes aren't moving!

1237
01:10:43,500 --> 01:10:44,600
Okay, keep going!

1238
01:10:44,600 --> 01:10:46,680
Is there a VR-exclusive too?

1239
01:10:46,680 --> 01:10:49,820
A VR version of this would be way too much.

1240
01:10:49,820 --> 01:10:53,140
Let's go!

1241
01:10:53,140 --> 01:10:56,260
Okay, number 4, number 4!

1242
01:10:56,260 --> 01:11:00,560
Moving forward.

1243
01:11:00,560 --> 01:11:06,940
Did the guy come at a normal speed?

1244
01:11:06,940 --> 01:11:10,440
The guy appeared!

1245
01:11:10,440 --> 01:11:11,680
But when you're just staring at everything like this—

1246
01:11:11,680 --> 01:11:14,260
Just scanning everything constantly—

1247
01:11:14,260 --> 01:11:16,320
Like the eyeball on the poster too,

1248
01:11:16,320 --> 01:11:23,360
Or a missing door — you'd definitely forget about that one.

1249
01:11:23,360 --> 01:11:35,650
Oujitan is here!

1250
01:11:35,650 --> 01:11:41,570
What was it — something like Nigottan's transition was like "hold on a sec"?

1251
01:11:41,570 --> 01:11:46,750
Like "there's no such thing~" or something? What was it?

1252
01:11:46,750 --> 01:11:53,420
What was it — something like "just wait a nyaan"?

1253
01:11:53,420 --> 01:11:58,400
Okay okay, number 5. Oh right, and then there's Doshintania.

1254
01:11:58,400 --> 01:12:06,060
I don't think it was this drawn-out. And that's Doshintania — wait, that's Riona's.

1255
01:12:06,060 --> 01:12:18,830
For the crime of mixing up my kouhai's transitions, Polka will press forward. I'll carry this with me.

1256
01:12:18,830 --> 01:12:23,490
It's the Tile Man!

1257
01:12:23,490 --> 01:12:27,680
Tile Man is standing by.

1258
01:12:27,680 --> 01:12:37,320
Tile Man is standing by directly behind me.

1259
01:12:37,320 --> 01:12:41,500
How close can I get to this thing?

1260
01:12:41,500 --> 01:12:54,240
I'm moving closer so everyone can see. I'm zooming in right now.

1261
01:12:54,240 --> 01:13:02,980
Okay I'm done, scary scary scary scary scary scary scary!

1262
01:13:02,980 --> 01:13:06,600
Sorry, sorry — I chickened out. The chicken has landed.

1263
01:13:06,600 --> 01:13:09,100
Sorry, I chickened out.

1264
01:13:09,100 --> 01:13:11,760
Chicken! Total chicken! I'm done.

1265
01:13:11,760 --> 01:13:21,670
I knocked over the water — wait, I knocked over the diffuser too by mistake. I'm done.

1266
01:13:21,670 --> 01:13:26,470
Sorry, Pachin.

1267
01:13:26,470 --> 01:13:29,470
Wait, was it Pachin? Pachin? Was it Pachin?

1268
01:13:29,470 --> 01:13:31,220
Sorry, Pachin.

1269
01:13:31,220 --> 01:13:34,000
Okay!

1270
01:13:34,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Hmm... no smoking.

1271
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:37,800
Two of them.

1272
01:13:37,800 --> 01:13:40,500
Umm...

1273
01:13:40,500 --> 01:13:42,540
Normal poster.

1274
01:13:42,540 --> 01:13:44,520
Looks normal...

1275
01:13:44,520 --> 01:13:45,140
Guy looks normal.

1276
01:13:45,140 --> 01:13:47,520
Normal guy.

1277
01:13:47,520 --> 01:13:49,400
Hmm...

1278
01:13:49,400 --> 01:13:54,740
The ceiling is already—

1279
01:13:54,740 --> 01:13:56,020
Gone, good.

1280
01:13:56,020 --> 01:13:57,940
Floor tiles — okay, okay, okay!

1281
01:13:57,940 --> 01:14:00,200
Wait, an eyeball?

1282
01:14:00,200 --> 01:14:11,440
Why is it coming from here?

1283
01:14:11,440 --> 01:14:13,480
That's an instant game over!

1284
01:14:13,480 --> 01:14:27,750
I already saw it.

1285
01:14:27,750 --> 01:14:30,250
Only people who've already seen it can get past this point.

1286
01:14:30,250 --> 01:14:33,250
Why does Polka-n let her guard down?

1287
01:14:33,250 --> 01:14:37,250
Here we go!

1288
01:14:37,250 --> 01:14:38,330
Okay!

1289
01:14:38,330 --> 01:14:42,320
Tonight's gonna be a long night.

1290
01:14:42,320 --> 01:14:47,130
It's fine.

1291
01:14:47,130 --> 01:14:49,830
It's fine.

1292
01:14:49,830 --> 01:14:52,010
It's fine.

1293
01:14:52,010 --> 01:14:55,570
It's fine.

1294
01:14:55,570 --> 01:14:58,820
Alright!

1295
01:14:58,820 --> 01:15:06,240
Nice, nice, nice!

1296
01:15:06,240 --> 01:15:06,920
Moving on!

1297
01:15:06,920 --> 01:15:16,330
Polka was in some kind of...

1298
01:15:16,330 --> 01:15:18,750
mysterious "I want to miss things" mode, wasn't she?

1299
01:15:18,750 --> 01:15:25,080
The guy looks normal.

1300
01:15:25,080 --> 01:15:33,820
It says to turn back, so...

1301
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:35,820
I'll follow the instructions as instructed.

1302
01:15:35,820 --> 01:16:07,860
Alright, checking, checking, checking — okay! Oh wait, it's stretching! Good thing I noticed early. When you're looking at other stuff, you can miss things, right? Like the poster.

1303
01:16:11,580 --> 01:16:17,140
Goodbye!

1304
01:16:17,140 --> 01:16:22,800
But from inside the poster...

1305
01:16:22,800 --> 01:16:23,340
like...

1306
01:16:23,340 --> 01:16:26,660
there aren't really any anomalies that directly harm Polka,

1307
01:16:26,660 --> 01:16:28,800
so that's a relief.

1308
01:16:28,800 --> 01:16:30,380
Exit 8 is a blessing.

1309
01:16:30,380 --> 01:16:37,430
There are some scary moments,

1310
01:16:37,430 --> 01:16:39,490
and chase sequences pop up sometimes,

1311
01:16:39,490 --> 01:16:40,890
but it doesn't really do anything

1312
01:16:40,890 --> 01:16:42,910
that bad to Polka,

1313
01:16:42,910 --> 01:16:46,270
so Exit 8...

1314
01:16:46,270 --> 01:16:50,480
maybe that's why it was so well-loved.

1315
01:16:50,480 --> 01:16:52,970
There are tons of Exit 8-likes out there now, right?

1316
01:16:52,970 --> 01:16:54,010
Anyway!

1317
01:16:54,010 --> 01:17:02,610
I love the random elements too,

1318
01:17:02,610 --> 01:17:03,240
the gacha aspect.

1319
01:17:03,240 --> 01:17:06,290
Here we go!

1320
01:17:06,290 --> 01:17:12,750
Lights — OK!

1321
01:17:12,750 --> 01:17:15,290
Floor — OK!

1322
01:17:15,290 --> 01:17:16,530
Poster...

1323
01:17:16,530 --> 01:17:19,130
Poster — OK!

1324
01:17:19,130 --> 01:17:21,830
Doorknob, doorknob, doorknob — OK!

1325
01:17:21,830 --> 01:17:23,870
Wait, hold on, mister.

1326
01:17:23,870 --> 01:17:24,770
I wasn't looking at the guy.

1327
01:17:24,770 --> 01:17:26,390
Sorry, I wasn't watching you, mister.

1328
01:17:26,390 --> 01:17:29,550
Eyes...

1329
01:17:29,550 --> 01:17:30,370
OK!

1330
01:17:30,370 --> 01:17:31,930
OK, OK, OK!

1331
01:17:31,930 --> 01:17:33,550
All OK!

1332
01:17:33,550 --> 01:17:34,790
Alright!

1333
01:17:34,790 --> 01:17:39,380
But gacha is

1334
01:17:39,380 --> 01:17:41,580
super popular overseas too —

1335
01:17:41,580 --> 01:17:42,920
it's a worldwide gacha culture.

1336
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:44,260
Moving on!

1337
01:17:44,260 --> 01:17:46,080
Okay!

1338
01:17:46,080 --> 01:17:49,980
Oh no, wait.

1339
01:17:49,980 --> 01:17:51,680
I thought the guy sped up just now.

1340
01:17:51,680 --> 01:17:53,860
No, he's at normal speed.

1341
01:17:53,860 --> 01:18:00,180
Normal guy.

1342
01:18:00,180 --> 01:18:03,310
Normal door.

1343
01:18:03,310 --> 01:18:05,050
Three of them.

1344
01:18:05,050 --> 01:18:06,930
Behind — normal.

1345
01:18:06,930 --> 01:18:08,530
Tiles — normal.

1346
01:18:08,530 --> 01:18:16,930
Oh no, oh no!

1347
01:18:16,930 --> 01:18:17,870
Oh nooo!

1348
01:18:17,870 --> 01:18:21,010
Even when you know it's coming, you still scream, right?

1349
01:18:21,010 --> 01:18:25,170
Not normal anymore!

1350
01:18:25,170 --> 01:18:27,830
Exit 8 — a game for growth.

1351
01:18:27,830 --> 01:18:32,430
Here I go.

1352
01:18:32,430 --> 01:18:32,790
Okay!

1353
01:18:32,790 --> 01:18:38,900
Looks normal?

1354
01:18:38,900 --> 01:18:45,270
That's a bang, right?

1355
01:18:45,270 --> 01:18:50,300
Not a freeze effect.

1356
01:18:50,300 --> 01:18:55,950
Probably not.

1357
01:18:55,950 --> 01:18:58,430
If there's a tile man lurking at the corner here...

1358
01:18:58,430 --> 01:19:01,490
that would be intense.

1359
01:19:01,490 --> 01:19:02,990
He did peek out a little earlier though.

1360
01:19:02,990 --> 01:19:04,150
There it is!

1361
01:19:04,150 --> 01:19:13,490
This time it's really over, thank goodness.

1362
01:19:13,490 --> 01:19:17,360
Alright!

1363
01:19:17,360 --> 01:19:20,360
Can I get out? Is this it?

1364
01:19:20,360 --> 01:19:22,460
Can I seriously get out?

1365
01:19:22,460 --> 01:19:26,840
I think it's here!

1366
01:19:26,840 --> 01:19:28,860
Nope, it's not here.

1367
01:19:28,860 --> 01:19:31,980
No door! No door! There's no door!

1368
01:19:31,980 --> 01:19:42,340
Turn back.

1369
01:19:42,340 --> 01:19:46,400
Ugh, when am I ever getting out of here? Okay, for now—

1370
01:19:46,400 --> 01:19:57,490
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

1371
01:19:57,490 --> 01:20:01,990
Found the exit, found the exit, gotta get home fast, couldn't find the exit—

1372
01:20:01,990 --> 01:20:05,810
That CM was hilarious — Nino kept checking on the old man,

1373
01:20:05,810 --> 01:20:10,070
like "old man, old man, old man, old man" over and over, it was so funny.

1374
01:20:10,070 --> 01:20:12,070
I'm doing the same thing.

1375
01:20:12,070 --> 01:20:12,550
Old man.

1376
01:20:12,550 --> 01:20:13,410
Old man.

1377
01:20:13,410 --> 01:20:14,670
Old man.

1378
01:20:14,670 --> 01:20:15,590
Old man.

1379
01:20:15,590 --> 01:20:23,840
I really want to see the movie soon.

1380
01:20:23,840 --> 01:20:24,580
Moving on.

1381
01:20:24,580 --> 01:20:32,620
Is this really it?

1382
01:20:32,620 --> 01:20:34,760
Is this really—

1383
01:20:34,760 --> 01:20:35,420
Is it here?

1384
01:20:35,420 --> 01:20:39,670
Is this—

1385
01:20:39,670 --> 01:20:43,450
What do you think? Is this really it?

1386
01:20:43,450 --> 01:20:44,450
Huh?

1387
01:20:44,450 --> 01:20:47,550
Seriously?

1388
01:20:47,550 --> 01:20:50,350
It was normal.

1389
01:20:50,350 --> 01:21:00,620
Okay!

1390
01:21:00,620 --> 01:21:03,940
Thank you!

1391
01:21:03,940 --> 01:21:06,820
I made it out!

1392
01:21:06,820 --> 01:21:11,420
Well then, The Exit 8 with all its new elements was a lot of fun!

1393
01:21:11,420 --> 01:21:15,220
Don't put a drain there, you'll ruin the vibe of the ending!

1394
01:21:15,220 --> 01:21:16,860
Anyway, that's a wrap!

1395
01:21:16,860 --> 01:21:18,820
The real, true—

1396
01:21:18,820 --> 01:21:25,380
I haven't dropped anything yet.

1397
01:21:25,380 --> 01:21:26,480
At this point, still—

1398
01:21:26,480 --> 01:21:29,100
Play the ambient sounds, hurry up!

1399
01:21:29,100 --> 01:21:30,620
Just a little more—

1400
01:21:30,620 --> 01:21:32,500
One step at a time.

1401
01:21:32,500 --> 01:21:33,560
And now—

1402
01:21:33,560 --> 01:21:34,960
Omaru Polka—

1403
01:21:34,960 --> 01:21:38,960
—from underground to the outside world—

1404
01:21:38,960 --> 01:21:39,460
Now—

1405
01:21:39,460 --> 01:21:41,590
Oh!

1406
01:21:41,590 --> 01:21:52,960
She sets foot on solid ground!

1407
